data srv4_bmc_fan_projection_probe_note: String = "Authenticated BMC SSH, 2026-07-30: srv4's config-asrr.json was rebuilt to the srv3 2.07.00 vendor stock aggressive curve by running the modeled TEMP_SOC jq realization on srv4's pre-onboarding base config and writing the canonical bytes back through a staged same-filesystem atomic rename; the live digest read back equal to altrad8ud_openbmc_322_fleet_quiet_projected_config_sha256_hex. srv4_bmc_fan_convergence_receipt is the typed live receipt of the converged state (12 samples over 120 seconds, TEMP_SOC 60-63C, guarded component max 69C, aggregate FAN1 4600 RPM). This replaces the earlier 2026-07-27 lazy-curve projection provenance."

data bmc_historical_receipt_not_realization_identity_note: String = "These July 30 rows are immutable historical evidence snapshots, not live producers and not StateDurabilityEvidence. In particular BmcFanConvergenceReceipt deliberately has no StateRealizationIdentity: the content-addressed SymbolIndex subtree-digest authority does not exist yet, so std.state_durability exposes only counted CallerAssertedDefinitionLinkage rows and refuses durable qualification. Hashing a remembered label or these observed output values would leave definition changes invisible; these historical rows therefore do not pretend to supply realization linkage."

data srv4_bmc_fan_reboot_persistence_note: String = "Live perturbation receipt, 2026-07-30 (aggressive stock curve): Redfish Manager.Reset advertised and accepted GracefulRestart with HTTP 200. The BMC was observed down for a 170-second reachability interval while srv4's host OS remained up (ComputerSystem PowerState On). After return, OpenBMC still reported 3.22.00; the active config-asrr.json SHA-256 digest was unchanged and equal to the srv3 stock aggressive curve projection (f559aff7...); phosphor-pid-control was active; zone0 FailSafe=false. This proves the JFFS2 upper override persists the aggressive curve across one graceful BMC restart. It does not prove persistence across a firmware replacement."

data fleet_bmc_surface_observation_note: String = "Authenticated read-only Redfish observations, 2026-07-27. srv3 OpenBMC 2.07.00 advertises ThermalSubsystem and its 51-member Chassis/Sensors collection includes temperature and fan readings; the legacy Chassis/Thermal URI is absent. srv4 OpenBMC 3.22.00 advertises legacy Chassis/Thermal; its Chassis/Sensors request still returns HTTP success but has only 9 power/utilization members and omits temperature/fan readings. A collection-only observer therefore fails open on srv4: transport success is not telemetry completeness. Direct known sensor URIs still resolve, but they do not make an inventory query complete."

data fleet_bmc_update_service_observation_note: String = "Authenticated read-only Redfish observations, 2026-07-27. Both srv3 2.07.00 and srv4 3.22.00 advertise /redfish/v1/UpdateService/update through HttpPushUri and MultipartHttpPushUri, and each active BMC image is Updateable=true. Each FirmwareInventory exposed exactly one BMC image plus non-BMC members; neither exposed a backup BMC image. This is update-surface capability evidence, not an approved image, apply receipt, or recovery proof."

data bmc_fan_symbol_index_subtree_digest_dissolve_on: std.dissolution.DissolutionCondition = std.dissolution.unbound_dissolution(description: "namespace content-addressed SymbolIndex subtree digest")
